---
import { slaterKosterSP, slaterKosterPP } from '../../../data/part04/ch14TeachingModels.mjs';

const componentId = 'ch14-slater-koster';
const defaults = { angle: 35, spSigma: 1.2, ppSigma: 1.6, ppPi: -0.4 };
const radians = defaults.angle * Math.PI / 180;
const l = Math.cos(radians);
const m = Math.sin(radians);
const sp = slaterKosterSP({ directionCosine: l, spSigma: defaults.spSigma });
const pp = slaterKosterPP({ l, m, ppSigma: defaults.ppSigma, ppPi: defaults.ppPi });
---

<figure class="chapter-visual sk-explorer" id={componentId}>
  <figcaption>
    <strong>原创交互模型：Slater–Koster 方向余弦</strong>
    <span lang="en">Original interactive model: Slater–Koster direction cosines</span>
  </figcaption>

  <label class="sk-explorer__control">
    <span>键方向 θ（degree）| Bond direction θ</span>
    <input data-sk-angle type="range" min="0" max="180" step="1" value={defaults.angle} />
    <output data-sk-angle-output>{defaults.angle}°</output>
  </label>

  <svg viewBox="0 0 680 320" role="img" aria-labelledby={`${componentId}-title ${componentId}-desc`}>
    <title id={`${componentId}-title`}>Bond orientation and representative Slater–Koster matrix elements</title>
    <desc id={`${componentId}-desc`}>A bond rotates in the xy plane. Direction cosines determine s-p and p-p matrix elements from fixed sigma and pi integrals.</desc>
    <line class="sk-explorer__axis" x1="340" y1="160" x2="610" y2="160" />
    <line class="sk-explorer__axis" x1="340" y1="160" x2="340" y2="35" />
    <circle cx="340" cy="160" r="18" class="sk-explorer__site" />
    <circle data-sk-end cx={340 + 170 * l} cy={160 - 170 * m} r="18" class="sk-explorer__site" />
    <line data-sk-bond x1="340" y1="160" x2={340 + 170 * l} y2={160 - 170 * m} class="sk-explorer__bond" />
    <path data-sk-arc d="M415 160 A75 75 0 0 0 401 117" class="sk-explorer__arc" />
    <text x="620" y="165">x</text>
    <text x="335" y="28">y</text>
    <text data-sk-theta x="415" y="125">θ={defaults.angle}°</text>
    <text x="70" y="70">l = cos θ</text>
    <text x="70" y="98">m = sin θ</text>
    <text x="70" y="145">⟨s|H|pₓ⟩ = l Vspσ</text>
    <text x="70" y="175">⟨pₓ|H|pᵧ⟩ = lm(Vppσ−Vppπ)</text>
    <text x="70" y="205">⟨pₓ|H|pₓ⟩ = l²Vppσ+(1−l²)Vppπ</text>
  </svg>

  <div class="chapter-visual__readout" aria-live="polite">
    <span data-sk-l>l={l.toFixed(3)}</span>
    <span data-sk-m>m={m.toFixed(3)}</span>
    <span data-sk-sp>spₓ={sp.toFixed(3)}</span>
    <span data-sk-ppxy>pₓpᵧ={pp.pxy.toFixed(3)}</span>
  </div>

  <div class="chapter-visual__contract">
    <p><strong>模型：</strong>键位于 xy 平面，<code>l=cosθ</code>、<code>m=sinθ</code>。固定 <code>Vspσ=1.2</code>、<code>Vppσ=1.6</code>、<code>Vppπ=−0.4</code>，使用声明的实 Cartesian p-orbital 符号规范。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Model:</strong> the bond lies in the xy plane with <code>l=cosθ</code> and <code>m=sinθ</code>. Fixed values are <code>Vspσ=1.2</code>, <code>Vppσ=1.6</code>, and <code>Vppπ=−0.4</code>, under the declared real Cartesian p-orbital sign convention.</p>
    <p><strong>验收：</strong>θ=0° 时 <code>spₓ=Vspσ</code>、<code>pₓpᵧ=0</code>、<code>pₓpₓ=Vppσ</code>；θ=90° 时 <code>spₓ=0</code>、<code>pₓpₓ=Vppπ</code>。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Acceptance:</strong> at θ=0°, <code>spₓ=Vspσ</code>, <code>pₓpᵧ=0</code>, and <code>pₓpₓ=Vppσ</code>; at θ=90°, <code>spₓ=0</code> and <code>pₓpₓ=Vppπ</code>.</p>
    <p><strong>边界：</strong>图只展示 two-centre 方向旋转；不包含多中心势、径向积分、环境依赖、overlap 或完整 d-orbital 表。轨道相位规范改变时，某些奇宇称矩阵元的符号会改变。</p>
    <p lang="en"><strong>Boundary:</strong> the figure shows only two-centre rotation. It omits multicentre potentials, radial integrals, environment dependence, overlap, and the full d-orbital table. Orbital phase conventions can change signs of odd-parity matrix elements.</p>
  </div>

  <noscript><p>关闭 JavaScript 后保留 θ=35° 的静态 bond orientation 与矩阵元。</p></noscript>
</figure>

<script>
  import { slaterKosterSP, slaterKosterPP } from '../../../data/part04/ch14TeachingModels.mjs';

  const root = document.getElementById('ch14-slater-koster');
  if (root) {
    const input = root.querySelector('[data-sk-angle]');
    const output = root.querySelector('[data-sk-angle-output]');
    const endpoint = root.querySelector('[data-sk-end]');
    const bond = root.querySelector('[data-sk-bond]');
    const theta = root.querySelector('[data-sk-theta]');
    const lOutput = root.querySelector('[data-sk-l]');
    const mOutput = root.querySelector('[data-sk-m]');
    const spOutput = root.querySelector('[data-sk-sp]');
    const ppxyOutput = root.querySelector('[data-sk-ppxy]');
    if (
      input instanceof HTMLInputElement
      && output instanceof HTMLOutputElement
      && endpoint instanceof SVGCircleElement
      && bond instanceof SVGLineElement
      && theta instanceof SVGTextElement
      && lOutput instanceof HTMLElement
      && mOutput instanceof HTMLElement
      && spOutput instanceof HTMLElement
      && ppxyOutput instanceof HTMLElement
    ) {
      const update = () => {
        const angle = Number(input.value);
        const radians = angle * Math.PI / 180;
        const l = Math.cos(radians);
        const m = Math.sin(radians);
        const x = 340 + 170 * l;
        const y = 160 - 170 * m;
        endpoint.setAttribute('cx', x.toFixed(2));
        endpoint.setAttribute('cy', y.toFixed(2));
        bond.setAttribute('x2', x.toFixed(2));
        bond.setAttribute('y2', y.toFixed(2));
        output.value = `${angle.toFixed(0)}°`;
        theta.textContent = `θ=${angle.toFixed(0)}°`;
        lOutput.textContent = `l=${l.toFixed(3)}`;
        mOutput.textContent = `m=${m.toFixed(3)}`;
        spOutput.textContent = `spₓ=${slaterKosterSP({ directionCosine: l, spSigma: 1.2 }).toFixed(3)}`;
        ppxyOutput.textContent = `pₓpᵧ=${slaterKosterPP({ l, m, ppSigma: 1.6, ppPi: -0.4 }).pxy.toFixed(3)}`;
      };
      input.addEventListener('input', update);
      update();
    }
  }
</script>

<style>
  .sk-explorer__control { display: grid; gap: 0.35rem; }
  .sk-explorer input, .sk-explorer svg { width: 100%; }
  .sk-explorer svg text { fill: currentColor; font-size: 13px; }
  .sk-explorer__axis { stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .sk-explorer__bond { stroke: var(--sl-color-accent-high); stroke-width: 4; }
  .sk-explorer__site { fill: var(--sl-color-accent-high); }
  .sk-explorer__arc { fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.4; }
</style>
